products=f'''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">NECore product architecture</span><h1>Three connected systems.<br>One stronger identity decision.</h1><p>Move beyond one-time checks with identity verification, continuous intelligence, and evidence-led compliance designed as one infrastructure layer.</p>{btn('Discuss your use case')}</div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="info-split" id="verification"><div><span class="eyebrow">Pillar 01 / Verification engine</span><h2>Confidence starts at the source.</h2><p>NECore's verification engine is designed to orchestrate identity-source lookups, document authenticity checks and specialist biometric services through authorized providers.</p><div class="feature-list"><div><b>Source verification</b> — NIN/BVN verification where legally authorized and commercially available.</div><div><b>Document processing</b> — OCR, document classification, authenticity evidence and exception handling.</div><div><b>Biometric assurance</b> — Licensed liveness and face-match services, with a human-review path.</div></div><p class="note-card">Government identity sources and specialist biometric checks require external approvals and provider agreements. Availability must be confirmed before production use.</p></div><div class="mini-visual"><div class="flow-card"><div><b>1 · Collect permitted information</b><small>Purpose, consent and required fields</small></div><span class="flow-num">01</span></div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>2 · Execute authorized checks</b><small>Source provider · document · liveness</small></div><span class="flow-num">02</span></div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>3 · Record an accountable result</b><small>Verified, rejected, or human review</small></div><span class="flow-num">03</span></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section alt" id="intelligence"><div class="container"><div class="info-split"><div class="blueprint"><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Identity context</b><small>Verification history and permitted signals</small></div><span class="state">Signal collected</span></div><div class="flow-arrow">↓</div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Risk analysis</b><small>Patterns, anomaly checks and device context</small></div><span class="state warn">Needs review</span></div><div class="flow-arrow">↓</div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Analyst action</b><small>Priority, explanation and evidence trail</small></div><span class="flow-num">03</span></div></div><div><span class="eyebrow">Pillar 02 / Intelligence layer</span><h2>Risk doesn't stop after onboarding.</h2><p>NECore's intelligence layer is designed to link identity signals over time, flag suspicious patterns, and support risk-tier changes for permitted monitoring use cases.</p><div class="feature-list"><div><b>Continuous scoring</b> — contextual risk tiers and policies, subject to validated models.</div><div><b>Behavioral anomalies</b> — unusual velocity, device and interaction patterns.</div><div><b>Cross-platform intelligence</b> — anonymized, lawful signals without unnecessary data disclosure.</div></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="compliance"><div class="container"><div class="info-split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Pillar 03 / Compliance infrastructure</span><h2>Make every decision explainable.</h2><p>Audit events, structured cases and controlled reporting create a traceable path from a verification request to the rationale behind a decision.</p><div class="feature-list"><div><b>Policy rules</b> — configurable identity and risk decisions with version history.</div><div><b>Human review</b> — exceptions, reason codes and independent approvals.</div><div><b>Evidence exports</b> — redacted reports and auditable event history.</div></div></div><div class="mini-visual"><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Verification evidence</b><small>Encrypted artifacts and source metadata</small></div><span class="flow-num">01</span></div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Compliance review</b><small>Risk tier, reasons and assigned analyst</small></div><span class="flow-num">02</span></div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Regulatory-ready record</b><small>Controlled export and policy history</small></div><span class="flow-num">03</span></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section alt" id="credentials"><div class="container"><div class="info-split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Phase 2 / Future capability</span><h2>An identity the customer can carry.</h2><p>The approved roadmap introduces portable, digitally signed credentials that users can hold and selectively share. Institutions verify the signed claims without repeatedly receiving raw identity numbers.</p><ul class="check-list"><li><span class="tick">✓</span>User-controlled disclosure and sharing duration.</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Standard public-key cryptography and signature verification.</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>No public blockchain or smart contracts required.</li></ul>{btn('Discuss roadmap access')}</div><div class="blueprint"><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Verified credential issued</b><small>Signed by NECore after authorized verification</small></div><span class="flow-num">01</span></div><div class="flow-arrow">↓</div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>User wallet stores credential</b><small>Keys and consent controlled on device</small></div><span class="flow-num">02</span></div><div class="flow-arrow">↓</div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Institution verifies proof</b><small>Cryptographic signature and valid status</small></div><span class="flow-num">03</span></div></div></div></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="container"><div class="cta-inner"><div><h2>Interested in a product walkthrough?</h2><p>Explore how NECore's three pillars could fit your institution's identity workflows.</p></div>{btn('Speak to our team','contact.html','light','btn-lg')}</div></div></section>'''
solutions=f'''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Solutions</span><h1>Identity confidence for the moments that matter.</h1><p>Whether you're onboarding customers, investigating anomalies or responding to a compliance request, the right information should be available to the right people.</p>{btn('Explore a pilot')}</div></section><section class="section"><div class="container">{section_header('Use cases','Built around institutional work.','NECore proposed platform is designed to support these common use cases as provider integrations and product modules become available.')}<div class="solution-grid">{''.join(f'<article class="solution-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon">{icon(ic,24)}</div><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></div></article>' for ic,title,text in [('bank','Banking and digital banks','Bring customer verification, decision evidence and human review into a structured onboarding workflow.'),('phone','Payments and fintech','Handle identity checks and escalations with a predictable integration contract.'),('briefcase','Compliance and risk teams','Track case ownership, exceptions, policy changes and evidence exports in one operational workspace.'),('globe','Digital platforms','Design reusable identity screening journeys without building every workflow from scratch.'),('network','Fraud investigations','Link permitted identity-related signals and investigate unusual patterns with a review trail.'),('user','Customer identity experiences','Offer clear consent, status updates and, in Phase 2, controlled sharing through signed credentials.')])}</div></div></section><section class="section alt"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Every role has a view</span><h2 class="section-title">One platform, clearly divided responsibilities.</h2><p class="desc">Customers, institutional teams, compliance reviewers and developers all need different interfaces. NECore is designed to connect their workflows while protecting boundaries between them.</p><ul class="check-list"><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Institution request and verification management.</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Risk analyst and compliance review with role controls.</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Customer-facing consent, submission and decision status.</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Developer integration tools and auditable delivery events.</li></ul></div>{flow_visual}</div></section><section class="cta"><div class="container"><div class="cta-inner"><div><h2>Let's map your identity journey.</h2><p>Share your organization, industry and workflow needs to explore a tailored demonstration.</p></div>{btn('Request a demo','contact.html','light')}</div></div></section>'''
developers=f'''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Built for developers</span><h1>Integrate verification.<br>Keep the full context.</h1><p>A proposed API-first architecture for creating verification requests, handling decision states and tracing outcomes. Public API access is planned and not yet available.</p>{btn('Request sandbox updates','contact.html')}</div></section><section class="section"><div class="container">{section_header('Integration model','Build once. Stay in control.','A consistent set of status transitions, signed events and idempotent requests can make verification integration more predictable.')}<div class="card-grid">{card('code','A coherent API contract','Create verification requests, retrieve status, and attach your customer reference for consistent case tracking.','contact.html','Discuss access')}{card('key','Scoped credentials','Separate test and production environments with least-privilege API keys and rotation.','security.html','Security model')}{card('file','Event-based outcomes','Use signed webhooks and stored delivery history to process outcomes safely.','security.html','Review evidence')}</div></div></section><section class="section alt" id="sandbox"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Illustrative API</span><h2 class="section-title">Predictable requests. Clear outcomes.</h2><p class="desc">The code on the right is a proposed interface—not a live integration or an issued API key. It will be finalized as the backend and provider agreements are implemented.</p><ul class="check-list"><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Provider-dependent checks selected per request.</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Consent reference and verification purpose recorded.</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Statuses can include pending, verified, declined and human review.</li></ul></div><div class="code-wrap"><div class="code-top"><span>Request payload · illustrative only</span><button class="copy-button" data-copy-target="dev-code">Copy</button></div><pre class="code-content" id="dev-code">POST /v1/verifications\nContent-Type: application/json\nIdempotency-Key: request-unique-id\n\n&#123;\n  "customer_reference": "CUST-84219",\n  "purpose": "account_onboarding",\n  "consent_reference": "CONSENT-001",\n  "checks": ["identity_source", "liveness"]\n&#125;\n\n<span class="comment">// Responses and endpoints subject to final API specification</span></pre></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container">{section_header('Documentation roadmap','A platform ready for serious integration.')}<div class="stat-grid">{''.join(f'<div class="stat-card"><b>{title}</b><p>{body}</p></div>' for title,body in [('API reference','Versioned endpoint and data model documentation.'),('Webhook guide','Signature verification, retries and delivery observability.'),('Sandbox test fixtures','Synthetic identities and deterministic sample responses.'),('Security guidance','Credential storage, least privilege and audit practices.'),('Status transitions','Clear definitions for pending, inconclusive and final decisions.'),('Support channels','Integration support and incident escalation process.')])}</div></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="container"><div class="cta-inner"><div><h2>Integrating identity into your product?</h2><p>Join the conversation about pilot integrations and the upcoming sandbox.</p></div>{btn('Request developer access','contact.html','light')}</div></div></section>'''
security=f'''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Security & trust</span><h1>Security should be visible in the architecture.</h1><p>NECore is designed around purpose-limited verification, clear accountability, minimal exposure of identity data, and independent review for consequential decisions.</p>{btn('Ask about security','contact.html')}</div></section><section class="section"><div class="container">{section_header('Security by design','Trust requires more than a badge.','These are design commitments for the platform. Certifications, formal audits and regulatory approvals will only be published after independent confirmation.')}<div class="card-grid">{card('lock','Protection of sensitive data','Encrypted storage and transport, masked attributes, retention controls and strict production access boundaries.','contact.html','Discuss safeguards')}{card('shield','Least-privilege access','Dedicated roles, tenant isolation and evidence access limited to authorized reviewers.','contact.html','Discuss controls')}{card('file','Immutable-style evidence trail','Append-only audit event patterns, reason codes, timestamps, model versions and controlled report exports.','contact.html','Discuss evidence')}</div></div></section><section class="section alt"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Responsible verification</span><h2 class="section-title">Never mistake uncertainty for approval.</h2><p class="desc">A temporary provider outage, inconclusive biometric outcome, or conflicting data should produce an explicit state—not a confident but ungrounded decision.</p><ul class="check-list"><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Inconclusive and high-risk cases remain reviewable.</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Consequential decisions can require independent approval.</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Reviewers can see the evidence and policy behind a conclusion.</li></ul></div><div class="mini-visual"><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Provider result unavailable</b><small>No verification claim issued</small></div><span class="state warn">Inconclusive</span></div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Risk exception detected</b><small>Evidence preserved and case routed</small></div><span class="state warn">Review</span></div><div class="flow-card"><div><b>Human decision recorded</b><small>Reviewer, policy and rationale captured</small></div><span class="state">Auditable</span></div></div></div></section><section class="section" id="privacy"><div class="container">{section_header('Privacy & accountability','A clear model for sensitive identity information.')}<div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><b>Purpose limitation</b><p>Collect and process only information necessary for a valid verification purpose, with a documented legal basis.</p></div><div class="stat-card"><b>Data minimization</b><p>Prefer masked claims and provider outcomes over unnecessary retransmission of raw identity numbers.</p></div><div class="stat-card"><b>Retention & rights</b><p>Design clear retention, deletion and data-subject request workflows subject to lawful recordkeeping duties.</p></div></div><p class="note-card" style="margin-top:29px">Important: NECore's compliance framework is being developed. Nothing on this page should be interpreted as a claim of completed NDPA, CBN, NIMC or ISO certification, regulatory approval, or live identity-source authorization.</p></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="container"><div class="cta-inner"><div><h2>Need to assess our security approach?</h2><p>Let's discuss architecture, legal dependencies and the controls required for your use case.</p></div>{btn('Speak to NECore','contact.html','light')}</div></div></section>'''
company=f'''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">The NECore story</span><h1>Identity is a beginning.<br>Trust is an ongoing responsibility.</h1><p>We are building identity and risk infrastructure for institutions that need to know more than whether a document looks legitimate.</p>{btn('Talk with us')}</div></section><section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Our mission</span><h2 class="section-title">Make trusted identity decisions clearer and more accountable.</h2><p class="desc">NECore's approved product vision joins three fundamental capabilities: the ability to verify who someone is, understand how identity-associated risk changes, and preserve evidence that regulatory and operational teams can trust.</p><p class="desc">The initial focus is the Nigerian financial-services ecosystem, with a modular architecture intended to support expansion into additional markets and identity contexts.</p></div>{flow_visual}</div></section><section class="section alt"><div class="container">{section_header('What guides the product','Three principles behind every workflow.')}<div class="card-grid">{card('shield','Confidence must be earned','Verification results should come from legitimate sources and approved specialists, not unsupported automation.','products.html')}{card('eye','Decisions should be legible','Reviewers and institutions should understand what contributed to a risk outcome.','security.html')}{card('hand','Identity should respect the user','Users should understand verification requests and, over time, control more of what they share.','products.html#credentials')}</div></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="container"><div class="cta-inner"><div><h2>Building something trust-sensitive?</h2><p>Share the challenge you're solving and explore opportunities to collaborate.</p></div>{btn('Start a conversation','contact.html','light')}</div></div></section>'''
pricing=f'''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Commercial access</span><h1>Pricing that follows the verification you need.</h1><p>NECore's pricing model and provider fees are being finalized. We won't invent transaction rates or offer commitments before they are approved.</p>{btn('Discuss pricing','contact.html')}</div></section><section class="section"><div class="container">{section_header('Engagement options','A practical path from discovery to integration.','The options below describe possible engagement formats, not confirmed price plans or service-level agreements.')}<div class="price-grid"><div class="price-card"><span class="pill">DISCOVER</span><h3>Solution discussion</h3><p>Identify verification requirements, operational dependencies and the right pilot scope.</p><span class="secondary-rule"></span><ul class="check-list"><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Workflow assessment</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Provider dependency review</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Preliminary integration plan</li></ul>{btn('Book a discussion','contact.html','ghost')}</div><div class="price-card featured"><span class="pill">EARLY ACCESS</span><h3>Pilot engagement</h3><p>Explore a scoped verification pilot using approved providers and agreed success measures.</p><span class="secondary-rule"></span><ul class="check-list"><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Defined proof-of-concept objectives</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Sandbox and test-case planning</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Security and compliance checkpoints</li></ul>{btn('Request pilot access')}</div><div class="price-card"><span class="pill">FUTURE</span><h3>Enterprise integration</h3><p>Commercial and operational terms to be established after the platform and provider integrations are validated.</p><span class="secondary-rule"></span><ul class="check-list"><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Custom verification flows</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>Institutional role management</li><li><span class="tick">✓</span>API, reporting and support terms</li></ul>{btn('Contact sales','contact.html','ghost')}</div></div></div></section><section class="section alt"><div class="container"><h2 class="section-title" style="margin-bottom:30px">Pricing questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does NECore have a public per-verification price?</summary><p>Not yet. Provider pricing, data-source entitlements, hosting, volume and compliance requirements must be validated before a reliable commercial rate can be published.</p></details><details><summary>Can we evaluate the experience before production?</summary><p>The proposed platform includes a synthetic-data sandbox and demo flows. Live identity checks require authorized external providers and approved access.</p></details><details><summary>Can we request a tailored commercial proposal?</summary><p>Yes, once NECore's team has confirmed the use case, integration requirements and available services.</p></details></div></div></section>'''
contact=f'''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Contact NECore</span><h1>Let's talk about identity trust.</h1><p>Tell us a little about your organization and the problem you're solving. We can use that context to discuss a potential pilot or integration.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container contact-grid"><div class="contact-info"><span class="eyebrow">Let's connect</span><h2 class="section-title">Build the right verification journey together.</h2><p>Whether you're an institution seeking verification infrastructure, a developer preparing an integration, or a potential partner, we'd like to understand your requirements.</p><div class="feature-list"><div><b>1.</b> Tell us what you need verified.</div><div><b>2.</b> Discuss technical and provider dependencies.</div><div><b>3.</b> Define next steps for a responsible pilot.</div></div><p class="note-card">The web form is fully designed. Email delivery must be configured by NECore before launch, using the server-side environment variables documented with this project.</p></div><div class="form-card"><h2>Request a conversation</h2><p>Only business contact details are requested here—never submit NIN, BVN, identity images or other sensitive documents.</p><form id="contact-form" autocomplete="on"><div class="form-grid"><div class="field"><label for="fullName">Full name *</label><input name="fullName" id="fullName" autocomplete="name" required minlength="2" maxlength="100" placeholder="Your full name"></div><div class="field"><label for="email">Work email *</label><input name="email" type="email" id="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="160" placeholder="you@company.com"></div><div class="field"><label for="company">Organization *</label><input name="company" id="company" autocomplete="organization" required maxlength="120" placeholder="Your organization"></div><div class="field"><label for="role">Your role</label><input name="role" id="role" maxlength="100" placeholder="Product, Risk, Engineering..."></div></div><div class="field"><label for="interest">What are you interested in? *</label><select name="interest" id="interest" required><option value="">Select an area</option><option>Verification engine</option><option>Risk intelligence</option><option>Compliance workflows</option><option>API & developer integration</option><option>Pilot partnership</option><option>General enquiry</option></select></div><div class="field"><label for="message">Tell us about your use case *</label><textarea name="message" id="message" required minlength="10" maxlength="2000" placeholder="What problem are you hoping to solve? (Please do not include identity numbers or documents.)"></textarea><span class="hint">Do not share government identification numbers, passwords or biometric details.</span></div><div class="field" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px;opacity:0" aria-hidden="true"><label for="website">Website</label><input name="website" id="website" autocomplete="off" tabindex="-1"></div><label style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:10px;font-size:12px;color:#536c84;line-height:1.6;margin:7px 0 23px"><input type="checkbox" name="agree" required style="margin-top:3px"> I understand that my business contact information will be used to respond to this enquiry.</label><button class="btn btn-primary" style="width:100%" type="submit" id="sendBtn">Send enquiry {icon('arrow',17)}</button><div class="form-response" id="form-response" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="form-disclaimer">If a delivery provider has not been configured yet, the form will tell you rather than pretending your request was sent.</p></form></div></div></section>'''

